From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:20:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: quiesce capture work and release sessions on close

Decoder queue setup can open a firmware session before vb2 imports any
DMABUFs. Closing after REQBUFS or STREAMON without a QBUF then skips
vdec_buf_cleanup(), leaving a firmware session behind. Repeated empty
MediaCodec start/stop cycles can exhaust the firmware's session limit.
Closing a decoder can also race with a firmware release-reference event
that queues delayed CAPTURE work after cancellation.

Disable and drain delayed CAPTURE work before teardown, so firmware
callbacks cannot queue it again. Release a remaining firmware session
if there are no prepared buffers; otherwise let m2m context release
run the normal buffer cleanup. Use the same session-release helper in
both paths so an empty started session also stops, unloads its resources
and frees its internal buffers.

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View integration
Source: https://github.com/isilweo/linux/commit/d57feaf4fe518acdcb2de9eb30a4e8363b7edfec
Base-commit: 1c1a919fd728c881e7ccaf3cf18a3cf3055e0429
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
@@ -1921,6 +1921,12 @@ static int vdec_close(struct file *file)
 	vdec_pm_get(inst);
 	vdec_eos_cancel(inst);
-	cancel_work_sync(&inst->delayed_process_work);
+	/* Firmware callbacks during teardown must not queue the work again. */
+	disable_work_sync(&inst->delayed_process_work);
+
+	/* Unprepared DMABUF buffers never reach vdec_buf_cleanup(). */
+	if (!inst->buf_count && inst->state != INST_UNINIT)
+		vdec_session_release(inst);
+
 	venus_close_common(inst, file);
 	ida_destroy(&inst->dpb_ids);
 	vdec_pm_put(inst, false);
-- 
